WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.720
Crown immunity.

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:04.272
The government cannot be held liable.

00:00:04.272 --> 00:00:08.238
At common law, the Crown can only be sued with its own consent.

00:00:08.238 --> 00:00:16.329
The Crown Liability and Proceedings Act partially waives this immunity, allowing tort claims against the federal government in limited circumstances.

00:00:16.329 --> 00:00:23.590
But the waiver is partial, the liability is limited, and the Crown retains immunities that no private citizen or corporation enjoys.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:30.613
When the Auditor General finds that the government wasted billions on failed programs, there is no mechanism to recover taxpayer money.

00:00:30.613 --> 00:00:39.079
When the Ethics Commissioner finds a conflict of interest violation, the maximum penalty is a modest fine — not imprisonment, not removal from office.

00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:48.295
When courts rule that government action was unreasonable, the remedy is declaratory — the court says it was wrong but cannot impose damages that would create meaningful deterrence.

00:00:48.295 --> 00:00:52.056
Crown immunity is the legal bedrock of zero accountability.

00:00:52.056 --> 00:00:58.261
It is the reason the accountability scorecard shows ten oversight bodies and zero enforcement outcomes.

00:00:58.261 --> 00:01:02.693
The four pillars of Crown immunity that prevent meaningful government accountability.

00:01:02.693 --> 00:01:04.443
Applied immunity.

00:01:04.443 --> 00:01:09.249
How Crown immunity has protected the government in documented cases across this site.

00:01:09.249 --> 00:01:12.170
The legal bedrock of zero accountability.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.897
Crown immunity is not one layer of the system architecture.

00:01:15.897 --> 00:01:19.272
It is the bedrock on which every other layer rests.

00:01:19.272 --> 00:01:24.454
The oversight bodies cannot enforce because the Crown is immune from meaningful consequence.

00:01:24.454 --> 00:01:29.102
Courts cannot check executive power effectively because remedies are declaratory.

00:01:29.102 --> 00:01:33.409
Officials cannot be held personally accountable because of qualified immunity.

00:01:33.409 --> 00:01:38.363
The financial cost of government failure is borne by taxpayers, not by the government.

00:01:38.363 --> 00:01:48.079
This is why the accountability scorecard shows ten oversight bodies and zero enforcement: the legal system is designed so that finding a violation does not produce a consequence.

00:01:48.079 --> 00:01:53.159
The Crown that commits the violation is the same Crown that must consent to being held liable.

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:55.124
It does not consent.

00:01:55.124 --> 00:02:02.215
The system architecture documented across this site exists because the legal foundation makes accountability structurally impossible.
